**Supersedes the patch above** (comment 6623860245, branch head `49950cb62`): your retest found a real hole in it, and this rework closes it. Thank you for testing it on the real gateway — the 404 capture is what pinned the fix.

## What's wrong with the first patch

The retry treated *any* answer that wasn't 401/403 as "this header worked". Your vendor answers `x-api-key` alone with **404 `AUTH_KEY_MISSING`** — a header it doesn't take at all — so the first patch learned `x-api-key`, handed the 404 back, and left every model on the provider broken until the file was edited. The trigger was right; the learn was too wide, exactly as you said.

## The fix (patch below, 2 commits)

- `RetryOneAuth` now learns only a **2xx** answer (your narrowing): a header the vendor doesn't take (404) or an outage (5xx) is not learned, and the next header is asked before the answer goes back. On your gateway: 403 → `x-api-key` alone (404, not learned) → `Authorization` alone (200) → `authHeader: "bearer"` kept — your trace, reproduced by a test.
- The **model list** had the same two gaps and is fixed in the same commit: it learned on not-401/403 too, and it never retried on the #5021 403 "invalid api-key" refusal at all (only on the outright 401), so a provider on such a vendor couldn't fetch its list to begin with. It now retries on both refusals and learns only an answer.

## Verification

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| New `TestRetryOneAuth404NotLearned` (your retest trace: 403 → 404 not learned → 200 learns bearer) | red before the fix (the 404 was learned and returned), ok after |
| New `TestList404NotLearned` (same vendor shape on the model list) | red before the fix (list failed outright on the 403), ok after |
| Existing `TestRetryOneAuth*`, `TestBothAuthRefused`, `TestAuthKeyRefused`, `TestAuthHeaderChoice`, `TestListLearnsOneAuth` | ok |
| Ablation: product files (`authheader.go`, `live.go`) back at the parent, tests kept | both new tests red |
| `go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/provider ./internal/catalog` | ok (provider 136s, catalog 4.8s) |
| `gofmt -l`, `go vet`, `go build ./...` | clean (known `dockflap`/`trayimage` cgo warnings only) |
| `git am -3` onto current `main` (`0ee424e3e`) in a clean tree | applies clean; targeted tests pass there |

## Not verified

No request against your gateway itself — the 403/404 shapes are reproduced from your curl table as test fixtures; the vendor's answers beyond that table (e.g. whether `AUTH_KEY_MISSING` ever comes with a different status) are not covered.

